  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Resistance are connected in a meter bridge circuit as shown in the figure. The balancing length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. Now an unknown resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is connected in series with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and new balancing length is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> measured from the same end. Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/479d12ea-d21b-4c71-922e-e326f818711f-image_alt.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 141px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "20",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Applying balanced condition for meter bridge</p><p>Initially, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Finally, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>Q</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Dividing equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math> by (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>P</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
